, let's examine each expression. \n\n- Expression I is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\n- Expression II is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{6}$ only.\n\n- Expression III is also a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{6}$ only. Note that a statistic doesn't need to include every sample element.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0717ebb9-5fd9-5b4c-acc5-d9a8ab6e92d2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0717ebb9-5fd9-5b4c-acc5-d9a8ab6e92d2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0717ebb9-5fd9-5b4c-acc5-d9a8ab6e92d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e974b83-28b6-5e89-995d-50a977968dc8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4e0c5de3-7c79-5b7e-a720-d262f7cd52f4" "answer-111f2a1e-49a4-5425-9c30-77e8f10a7813" "answer-4e974b83-28b6-5e89-995d-50a977968dc8" "answer-7a32c857-a580-5328-90f1-f1b03c19902c" "answer-4fbcabc8-67e3-58c7-ada3-e4560b3ebf7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e0c5de3-7c79-5b7e-a720-d262f7cd52f4" :answer/id #uuid "4e0c5de3-7c79-5b7e-a720-d262f7cd52f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-111f2a1e-49a4-5425-9c30-77e8f10a7813" :answer/id #uuid "111f2a1e-49a4-5425-9c30-77e8f10a7813" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e974b83-28b6-5e89-995d-50a977968dc8" :answer/id #uuid "4e974b83-28b6-5e89-995d-50a977968dc8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a32c857-a580-5328-90f1-f1b03c19902c" :answer/id #uuid "7a32c857-a580-5328-90f1-f1b03c19902c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fbcabc8-67e3-58c7-ada3-e4560b3ebf7f" :answer/id #uuid "4fbcabc8-67e3-58c7-ada3-e4560b3ebf7f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f3ea39b0-84ca-56ad-ab8f-d5ad95ed12c9" :question/id #uuid "f3ea39b0-84ca-56ad-ab8f-d5ad95ed12c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-149836" :question/problem "Suppose the following data are sampled from a population.\n\n$$\n11,\\,16,\\,17,\\,25,\\,19,\\,18\n$$\n\nCalculate the value of the following statistic for this particular sample.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{max}({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n})-\\text{min}({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n})}{n+1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nNote the following notation:\n\n- ${X}_{i}$ denotes the random variable representing the $i$th observation in a random sample, and\n\n- ${x}_{i}$ is the value of ${X}_{i}$ in a specific sample.\n\nFor the given sample, we have\n\n- $\\text{max}({x}_{1},…,{x}_{6})=25,$\n\n- $\\text{min}({x}_{1},…,{x}_{6})=11.$\n\nTherefore, the value of our statistic for this particular sample is \n\n$$\n\\frac{25-11}{7}=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0441c25d-082e-5515-be23-e5ff8b2362c7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0441c25d-082e-5515-be23-e5ff8b2362c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "0441c25d-082e-5515-be23-e5ff8b2362c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a6aa4ba2-acdb-5a8f-a24e-648f0afd7f82" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b151b538-2cc8-5500-a1b6-cb843a708f46" "answer-a6aa4ba2-acdb-5a8f-a24e-648f0afd7f82" "answer-75b1e3b4-85ba-5f8a-bf46-da36377f8115" "answer-0ca9c9f0-589c-52d3-a8c1-fba9d48743bf" "answer-c8612a24-1b0a-52bb-b497-27d3e19bddfb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b151b538-2cc8-5500-a1b6-cb843a708f46" :answer/id #uuid "b151b538-2cc8-5500-a1b6-cb843a708f46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6aa4ba2-acdb-5a8f-a24e-648f0afd7f82" :answer/id #uuid "a6aa4ba2-acdb-5a8f-a24e-648f0afd7f82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75b1e3b4-85ba-5f8a-bf46-da36377f8115" :answer/id #uuid "75b1e3b4-85ba-5f8a-bf46-da36377f8115" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ca9c9f0-589c-52d3-a8c1-fba9d48743bf" :answer/id #uuid "0ca9c9f0-589c-52d3-a8c1-fba9d48743bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8612a24-1b0a-52bb-b497-27d3e19bddfb" :answer/id #uuid "c8612a24-1b0a-52bb-b497-27d3e19bddfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dea03ebf-107d-593b-bf22-bd12e437ac5e" :question/id #uuid "dea03ebf-107d-593b-bf22-bd12e437ac5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-139810" :question/problem "Suppose the following data are sampled from a population.\n\n$$\n12,\\,14,\\,9,\\,13,\\,12\n$$\n\nCalculate the value of the statistic $\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({X}_{i}-12)^{2}$ for this particular sample." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nNote the following notation:\n\n- ${X}_{i}$ denotes the random variable representing the $i$th observation in a random sample, and\n\n- ${x}_{i}$ is the value of ${X}_{i}$ in a specific sample.\n\nFor the given sample, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}({x}_{i}-12)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}((12-12)^{2}+(14-12)^{2}+(9-12)^{2}+(13-12)^{2}+(12-12)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(0+4+9+1+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(14) \\\\  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of our statistic for this particular sample is $2.8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-549a77fb-3799-53ea-8055-fff5234b161c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-549a77fb-3799-53ea-8055-fff5234b161c" :answer-field/id #uuid "549a77fb-3799-53ea-8055-fff5234b161c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ff489335-9af1-5d47-86f5-045b4f572698" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f20f7ac9-58e2-5c78-88f5-229f03713c78" "answer-ff489335-9af1-5d47-86f5-045b4f572698" "answer-a3031ea8-2e43-51ff-b2fd-30ea74be77fa" "answer-de2174f9-e529-576f-8bab-d4c0c5f7ac4d" "answer-2e37b817-af08-5d0b-9574-36430ff431e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f20f7ac9-58e2-5c78-88f5-229f03713c78" :answer/id #uuid "f20f7ac9-58e2-5c78-88f5-229f03713c78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff489335-9af1-5d47-86f5-045b4f572698" :answer/id #uuid "ff489335-9af1-5d47-86f5-045b4f572698" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3031ea8-2e43-51ff-b2fd-30ea74be77fa" :answer/id #uuid "a3031ea8-2e43-51ff-b2fd-30ea74be77fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de2174f9-e529-576f-8bab-d4c0c5f7ac4d" :answer/id #uuid "de2174f9-e529-576f-8bab-d4c0c5f7ac4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e37b817-af08-5d0b-9574-36430ff431e7" :answer/id #uuid "2e37b817-af08-5d0b-9574-36430ff431e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1599a91b-303e-58a8-b434-5ef4c1a036ef" :question/id #uuid "1599a91b-303e-58a8-b434-5ef4c1a036ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-139811" :question/problem "Suppose the following data are sampled from a population.\n\n$$\n2.25,\\,3.16,\\,2.65,\\,3.06,\\,2.94\n$$\n\nCalculate the value of the statistic $\\text{median}({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…{X}_{n})$ for this particular sample." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nNote the following notation:\n\n- ${X}_{i}$ denotes the random variable representing the $i$th observation in a random sample, and\n\n- ${x}_{i}$ is the value of ${X}_{i}$ in a specific sample.\n\nTo find the median for the given sample, we arrange the data in numerical order:\n\n$$\n2.25,\\,2.65,\\,2.94,\\,3.06,\\,3.16\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{median}({x}_{1},…,{x}_{5})=2.94.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of our statistic for this particular sample is $2.94.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd992445-9b24-5f2e-beb4-10cb760e8aed"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd992445-9b24-5f2e-beb4-10cb760e8aed" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd992445-9b24-5f2e-beb4-10cb760e8aed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-856acdf6-20ed-5add-91d0-4434a09e46d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-41c4124e-bec7-57ee-8cc8-21e077413d63" "answer-9b20a410-6d19-57e3-8648-d7bbbb0c29cb" "answer-856acdf6-20ed-5add-91d0-4434a09e46d4" "answer-5c159009-6903-5cb8-bc85-85d6ade859af" "answer-b3d41772-8e3a-5672-ab17-a843c0b39423"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41c4124e-bec7-57ee-8cc8-21e077413d63" :answer/id #uuid "41c4124e-bec7-57ee-8cc8-21e077413d63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b20a410-6d19-57e3-8648-d7bbbb0c29cb" :answer/id #uuid "9b20a410-6d19-57e3-8648-d7bbbb0c29cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.81" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-856acdf6-20ed-5add-91d0-4434a09e46d4" :answer/id #uuid "856acdf6-20ed-5add-91d0-4434a09e46d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.94" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c159009-6903-5cb8-bc85-85d6ade859af" :answer/id #uuid "5c159009-6903-5cb8-bc85-85d6ade859af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.06" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3d41772-8e3a-5672-ab17-a843c0b39423" :answer/id #uuid "b3d41772-8e3a-5672-ab17-a843c0b39423" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-264130f3-38ba-510d-80d5-15a003677fae" :question/id #uuid "264130f3-38ba-510d-80d5-15a003677fae" :question/math-academy-id "q-149837" :question/problem "The ages, in years, of six randomly selected college students drawn from a population were measured. The results are shown below.\n\n$$\n17,\\,19,\\,21,\\,18,\\,20,\\,19\n$$\n\nCalculate the value of the following statistic for this particular sample.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{min}({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n})+4}{n}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nNote the following notation:\n\n- ${X}_{i}$ denotes the random variable representing the $i$th observation in a random sample, and\n\n- ${x}_{i}$ is the value of ${X}_{i}$ in a specific sample.\n\nFor the given sample, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{min}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})=17\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of our statistic for this particular sample is $\\frac{17+4}{6}=3.5$ years." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f60edaef-c13b-5348-91f8-4e69a22c173f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f60edaef-c13b-5348-91f8-4e69a22c173f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f60edaef-c13b-5348-91f8-4e69a22c173f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5851829e-e164-50e4-a521-b2e5029611e8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-61f7e4c9-a328-59a5-8c5e-a513b1c8edcb" "answer-5851829e-e164-50e4-a521-b2e5029611e8" "answer-ab40a5fb-1670-5156-9f84-cc7d989d494a" "answer-9ca42f7b-82c6-5808-b73e-445211c3621a" "answer-f541b8c0-a1a1-5ebd-91a9-014ae312419a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61f7e4c9-a328-59a5-8c5e-a513b1c8edcb" :answer/id #uuid "61f7e4c9-a328-59a5-8c5e-a513b1c8edcb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2.3$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5851829e-e164-50e4-a521-b2e5029611e8" :answer/id #uuid "5851829e-e164-50e4-a521-b2e5029611e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3.5$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab40a5fb-1670-5156-9f84-cc7d989d494a" :answer/id #uuid "ab40a5fb-1670-5156-9f84-cc7d989d494a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3.8$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ca42f7b-82c6-5808-b73e-445211c3621a" :answer/id #uuid "9ca42f7b-82c6-5808-b73e-445211c3621a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f541b8c0-a1a1-5ebd-91a9-014ae312419a" :answer/id #uuid "f541b8c0-a1a1-5ebd-91a9-014ae312419a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$ years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188550 :question/problem "The heights, in meters, of six randomly selected children drawn from a population were measured. The results are shown below.\n\n$$\n1.34,\\,1.24,\\,1.42,\\,1.28,\\,1.39,\\,1.44\n$$\n\nCalculate the value of the statistic ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}$ for this particular sample." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nNote the following notation:\n\n- ${X}_{i}$ denotes the random variable representing the $i$th observation in a random sample, and\n\n- ${x}_{i}$ is the value of ${X}_{i}$ in a specific sample.\n\nFor the given sample, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}=1.34+1.24+1.42+1.28+1.39+1.44=8.11.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of our statistic for this particular sample is $8.11\\,\\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3be518d5-8e65-51e4-8c16-7752d6693d70"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3be518d5-8e65-51e4-8c16-7752d6693d70" :answer-field/id #uuid "3be518d5-8e65-51e4-8c16-7752d6693d70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e3fbe09-85be-535f-ad1f-23b1ff44f89f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b72f54bc-2f78-5a2a-a357-15c7b1e0a9b2" "answer-4e3fbe09-85be-535f-ad1f-23b1ff44f89f" "answer-3711c26b-4707-57d9-bc3a-ae24345bf877" "answer-8cfdabea-00d1-569e-bbdd-3b4970985102" "answer-8554a30d-6e9e-5d98-ae53-faadfb7e4fd6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b72f54bc-2f78-5a2a-a357-15c7b1e0a9b2" :answer/id #uuid "b72f54bc-2f78-5a2a-a357-15c7b1e0a9b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.01\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e3fbe09-85be-535f-ad1f-23b1ff44f89f" :answer/id #uuid "4e3fbe09-85be-535f-ad1f-23b1ff44f89f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.11\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3711c26b-4707-57d9-bc3a-ae24345bf877" :answer/id #uuid "3711c26b-4707-57d9-bc3a-ae24345bf877" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.24\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cfdabea-00d1-569e-bbdd-3b4970985102" :answer/id #uuid "8cfdabea-00d1-569e-bbdd-3b4970985102" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.28\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8554a30d-6e9e-5d98-ae53-faadfb7e4fd6" :answer/id #uuid "8554a30d-6e9e-5d98-ae53-faadfb7e4fd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.34\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186189366 :tutorial/content "Recall that, given a random sample $X_1, X_2,\\ldots X_n$ of size $n,$ the sample mean $\\overline{X}$ is an unbiased estimator of the population mean $\\mu,$ and is defined as\n\n$$\n\\overline{X} \n= \\dfrac1n\\sum_{i=1}^n X_i .\n$$\n\nThe sample mean is an example of a **statistic**. A statistic is a random variable computed using values from a sample. Statistics are often used to estimate population parameters, although they also have other uses.\n\nLet's take a look at some other examples of statistics:\n\n- The following statistic could be used as an estimator for the population variance $\\sigma^2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\dfrac1n \\sum_{i=1}^n (X_i - \\overline{X})^2\n$$\n\n- The following statistic could be used as an estimator for the population maximum:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{max}(X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_n)\n$$\n\n- The following statistic could be used as an estimator for the population range:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{max}(X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_n) - \\textrm{min}(X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_n)\n$$\n\n- The following statistic could be used as an estimator for the population median:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{median}(X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_n)\n$$\n\nStatistics cannot include any *unknown* population parameters. For example:\n\n- If the population mean $\\mu$ is *unknown,* then the following quantity is *not* a statistic:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\dfrac1n \\sum_{i=1}^n (X_i - \\mu)^2\n$$\n\n- However, if the population parameters $\\mu$ and $\\sigma$ are *both* known, then the following quantity *is* a statistic: \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle  \\sum_{i=1}^n \\left(\\dfrac{X_i - \\mu}{\\sigma}\\right)^2\n$$\n\nFinally, since statistics are described using observations from a random sample, they are random variables and therefore have a probability distribution. The probability distribution of a statistic is called the **sampling distribution** of the statistic." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188459 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
